Experiment 9(b): Matplotlib and Pandas

Aim:-
To write a Python program to implement Matplotlib and Pandas libraries.

Algorithm:-
1. Import Pandas and Matplotlib libraries.  
2. Create a dataset using a dictionary.  
3. Convert it into a DataFrame.  
4. Display the DataFrame.  
5. Plot a bar chart using Matplotlib.  
6. Add title and labels.  
7. Display the graph.  

Code:-
# Import libraries
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

# --------- NumPy Example ---------
print("NumPy Example:")

# Create a NumPy array
arr = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40, 50])
print("Array:", arr)

# Perform operations
print("Mean:", np.mean(arr))
print("Sum:", np.sum(arr))


# --------- Pandas Example ---------
print("\nPandas Example:")

# Create a dictionary
data = {
    "Name": ["A", "B", "C"],
    "Marks": [85, 90, 78]
}

# Convert to DataFrame
df = pd.DataFrame(data)

print("DataFrame:")
print(df)

# Display basic info
print("Average Marks:", df["Marks"].mean())

